  {
    "sha": "cd9b9a17c8a432c697574be54705d1c62f26f9dd",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGNkOWI5YTE3YzhhNDMyYzY5NzU3NGJlNTQ3MDVkMWM2MmYyNmY5ZGQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-16T06:04:28Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-16T06:04:28Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(fixtures): derive reference profiles only from STEP fixtures\n\nDeriveFixtureProfile replaced the generating profile of a DXF/profile\nfixture with a bulge-free derived polygon. The chord bound fell to zero,\nthe fixture became mesh-eligible, and mesh refinement cleared a real\ncollision with the intended curved steel. On an imported mesh fixture,\nlibrary re-insertion would re-mesh from the derived approximation.\n\nDerivation is now refused by name for every fixture without a STEP\nsource. Pinned by\ngenerated_fixture_refuses_reference_derivation_and_keeps_its_collision_bound,\nmesh_fixture_without_step_source_refuses_reference_derivation and\nmcp_derive_fixture_profile_refuses_generated_fixture_and_keeps_its_profile.\n\nRefs #744\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "5473408f4eab5a7a712ac258721d182251761c75",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/5473408f4eab5a7a712ac258721d182251761c75"
